+# ChromascopeIP
+
+**C++ image-processing laboratory | OpenCV 5.1.0 | Dear ImGui 1.93.0 | CLI + GUI**
+
+I rebuilt my 2020 *SkittlesIP* engineering-class project as a modern, extensible C++ application. This first baseline preserves the original four candy photographs while establishing a single processing core shared by a command-line application and a graphical desktop application.
+
+> **Current documentation:** [M10.8 user/maintainer documentation index](../DOCUMENTATION_INDEX.md)
+> describes the implemented GUI/CLI and its privacy, architecture and testing
+> boundaries. Historical M10.1–M10.7 issue notes below remain as development
+> records, not a statement that those features are unavailable today.
+
+## M12.7 — first-release documentation (Issue #90)
+
+The v1.0.0 candidate now has a [changelog](../CHANGELOG.md),
+[platform-specific installation guide](../INSTALLATION_1_0_0.md),
+[original reproducible examples](../RELEASE_EXAMPLES_1_0_0.md),
+[screenshot capture guidelines](../RELEASE_SCREENSHOTS_1_0_0.md), and
+[draft release notes](../RELEASE_NOTES_1_0_0.md). The [publication-readiness
+checklist](../M12_7_PUBLICATION_READINESS.md) gives a concrete path for
+resolving the outstanding M11.9 and M12.5 obligations before M12.8.
+Screenshots from a real GUI still need to be captured by the maintainer;
+**these documents do not authorize public publication**. M12.6's hosted
+second staging run was successful and retained five packages, five SBOMs and
+six signed attestation bundles. After M12.7, the *final* packages must be
+restaged and rehashed because installed documentation changes package contents.
+
+## M12.6 — v1.0.0 release staging and signed attestations (Issue #89)
+
+A manually dispatched, main-only [release staging workflow](../M12_6_RELEASE_STAGING.md)
+now reuses the full exact-source Release Candidate CI and prepares the five
+unmodified packages, CycloneDX drafts, `SHA256SUMS`, and a v1.0.0 **tag proposal**.
+A narrowly privileged staging job creates real GitHub Sigstore provenance and
+five package-specific SBOM attestations. **No tag, release or publication is
+performed.** The M11.9 redistribution review and M12.5 vulnerability/NOTICE
+findings remain genuine blockers to public release authorization; staging
+success does not waive them.
+
+## M12.4 — Windows 10/11 portable ZIP engineering acceptance (Issue #87)
+
+The maintainer reports successful manual extraction and GUI/CLI use of the
+ChromascopeIP 1.0.0 Windows x64 ZIP on Windows 10 and Windows 11. The existing
+MSVC native CTests, PE/CRT ZIP inspection, relocated CLI smoke, and full
+20-check Release Candidate CI remain the automated qualification evidence.
+See [M12.4 Windows ZIP acceptance](../M12_4_WINDOWS_ZIP_ACCEPTANCE.md).
+No new Windows JSON attestation files, historical commit reconstruction, or
+repetition of already completed testing is required for engineering sign-off.
+Physical-camera/codec coverage not reported remains unverified; M11.9
+redistribution clearance and public release approval remain separate.
+
+## M12.3 — four Linux clean-install VM acceptance (Issue #86)
+
+The maintainer reports successful fresh-VM installation and GUI/CLI testing on
+Debian 12/13 and Ubuntu 24.04/26.04. The existing distribution-specific APT
+smokes and same-run Release Candidate CI provide independent automated package
+evidence. See the [M12.3 clean-install acceptance guide](../M12_3_LINUX_CLEAN_INSTALL_ACCEPTANCE.md).
+The private nine-case JSON evidence tool is **optional**; generating four
+records or recovering old VM package digests is **not required for Issue #86
+engineering acceptance**. Exact correspondence between historical VM downloads
+and a particular CI source commit is not independently established. Unperformed
+checks must not be represented as passed. M11.9 redistribution review and
+final public-release approval remain separate, unresolved gates.
+
+## M12.2 — same-source final automated release-candidate matrix (Issue #85)
+
+`Release Candidate CI` reuses the complete native five-package matrix and
+Quality Release/sanitizer/clang-tidy suites in one run, then checks the
+artifact-matrix and review-required SBOM reports against the exact source SHA.
+Its evidence artifact explicitly **does not authorize** public redistribution,
+identify hardware certification, sign binaries or publish a tag. See the
+[M12.2 final RC matrix guide](../M12_2_FINAL_RC_MATRIX.md). The M11.9 human
+license/NOTICE review and outstanding M11.8 device sign-offs remain separate.
+
+## M12.1 — v1.0.0 version and feature-scope freeze (Issue #84)
+
+**Current source, GUI, CLI and five distribution filenames: 1.0.0.**
+This is a **release-candidate identity freeze, NOT a signed or published release**.
+The first-party v1.0 scope is frozen: local still-image tools, recorded video,
+explicit local object/person inference, opt-in live camera/temporary tracking,
+GUI, CLI, and five OS-specific distribution candidates. Model weights and
+unapproved historical media remain excluded; no networking, face recognition,
+or persistent identity tracking is introduced. Public release remains blocked
+on the unresolved M11.9 redistribution/NOTICE review, any missing M11.8
+manual-device attestations, and later release/signing gates. See the
+[M12.1 scope and version contract](../M12_1_RELEASE_SCOPE.md).
+
+## Current documentation (M10.8 / #74)
+
+**Start with the [current documentation index](../DOCUMENTATION_INDEX.md).**
+For day-to-day use: [GUI guide](../USER_GUIDE.md),
+[CLI reference](../CLI_REFERENCE.md),
+[local privacy/consent](../PRIVACY_GUIDE.md),
+[troubleshooting](../TROUBLESHOOTING.md), and
+[current system architecture](../CURRENT_ARCHITECTURE.md).
+The numbered milestone sections that follow preserve historical development
+snapshots; **older pending labels and capability tables are not current status**.
+At the accepted M10.7 baseline there are 147 native CTests, 28 camera-labeled
+CTests and 140 Python quality tests. M10.8 changes documentation and adds
+hardware-free documentation checks; it does **not** alter production behavior.
+
+> **Historical M8.4 foundation:** M8.1–M8.3 established native backend selection, passive discovery, validated formats, typed errors and bounded asynchronous capture. M8.4 adds a **user-activated local live-camera GUI workspace** with device selection, a visible capture indicator and Stop/session-reset cleanup. Still-image and recorded-video workflows remain intact. No automatic camera activation, recording, upload, face recognition or identity tracking is introduced. See [M8.4 camera preview](milestones/M8_4_CAMERA_GUI.md) and [privacy controls](milestones/M7_6_LOCAL_PRIVACY.md).
+
+## M11.1 installation and staging (Issue #75; accepted and merged)
+
+CMake now provides prefix-relative installation of the CLI, optional GUI,
+current documentation and model license/provenance **metadata**. Packages do
+**not** contain the historical Skittles JPEGs, videos, ONNX weights or native
+runtime libraries; those need separate rights/dependency qualification. GUI
+sample buttons remain available in a development checkout but are disabled
+when samples are absent in a relocated installation. See the
+[M11.1 installation guide](../M11_1_INSTALL_STAGING.md) for exact commands,
+`DESTDIR`, Windows configuration, relocatable layout, limitations and tests.
+This is a staging foundation, not a release-ready portable binary.
+
+## M11.2 Debian 12 AMD64 development package (Issue #76; accepted and merged)
+
+The Debian 12 pipeline builds and clean-install-smoke-tests an `amd64` `.deb`
+using the M11.1 install layout, the pinned OpenCV 5.1.0 private runtime and
+Debian-native dependency declarations. The historical M11.2 artifact was a pre-v1.0 development candidate.
+The **current M12.1 source is version 1.0.0 (release candidate only)**;
+no public v1.0.0 release has been authorized.
+The package retains attribution/license texts and omits historical sample media,
+ONNX weights and development dependencies. It must still pass CI, actual clean
+installation, later third-party release inventory and manual GUI/camera gates.
+See the [M11.2 Debian package guide](../M11_2_DEBIAN12_PACKAGE.md).
+
+## M11.3 Debian 13 AMD64 development package (Issue #77; accepted)
+
+Debian 13 (Trixie) builds a **separate** `amd64` package from its own pinned
+OpenCV 5.1.0 runtime and Trixie system-library dependency metadata, with the
+same M11.2 recursive OpenCV closure, private executable-relative ELF search
+paths, and procfs-aware clean-install checks. The current version-frozen candidate filename is
+`ChromascopeIP-1.0.0-Debian13-amd64.deb`; it remains **unpublished**. Debian 12 packaging continues independently. No original photos,
+recordings or ONNX model weights are bundled. See the [M11.3 Trixie package
+guide](../M11_3_DEBIAN13_PACKAGE.md) for acceptance limits.
+
+## M11.4 Ubuntu 24.04 AMD64 development package (Issue #78; accepted and merged)
+
+Ubuntu 24.04 (Noble) now constructs its own `ChromascopeIP-1.0.0-Ubuntu24.04-amd64.deb`
+using the native Noble toolchain, source-pinned OpenCV 5.1.0 and Ubuntu-generated
+APT dependencies. The CI check additionally installs the package into a fresh
